# Engines deliberately held at a spec commit the rest of the fleet has moved off.
# Read by scripts/fleet-spec-pin-check.mjs.
#
# One per line, `<repo>@<sha>: <reason>`. The reason is required: an exemption
# nobody can audit is how this gate would quietly stop meaning anything, so a
# bare repo name is an error rather than a skip. Every exemption that applies is
# printed on a passing run too, so what was waived stays visible.
#
# The sha is part of the key on purpose. An exemption naming only the repo
# outlives the divergence it describes and silences the next one; keyed on the
# pin, it stops applying the moment the pin moves. A line whose sha no longer
# matches, or whose engine has rejoined the fleet, is reported as an error
# telling you to delete it.
#
# Empty on purpose. The fleet agreeing is the normal state, and a divergence
# that nobody chose is the finding this gate exists for.
